# Rust build output
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Local player profile: identity keys, settings, hand history.
#
# The client is portable, so the profile lives next to the binary - which
# means it can appear at any depth, wherever somebody ran one. Unanchored
# for exactly that reason: `/profile/` matched the root only, and a client
# run from a tracked subdirectory would have written an unignored key pair.
profile/
/dist/

